B.aqi=s(["Red and round","Red and square","Blue and round","Blue and square"],t.s)
B.awy=s(["A red round card has two clues: red color and round shape. Both clues must match this group.","A red square card shares color with a red circle but has four equal sides in this model.","A blue round card shares shape with a red circle but not its color. One match is not two matches.","A blue square card belongs here only when both blue and square are true. Turning the card does not change its shape."],t.s)
B.aMs=s(["0|Where does a round red button drawing belong?","1|Where does a red card with four equal sides belong?","2|Where does a round blue lid drawing belong?","3|Where does a blue square tile drawing belong?","0|A circle is colored red. Which group satisfies both clues?","1|A square is red, not blue. Which group fits?","2|A blue card has no corners and a round outline. Which group fits?","3|A blue card has four equal straight sides and four square corners. Which group fits?","1|A card changes from blue to red but stays square. Which group fits now?","2|A red round card is recolored blue. Its shape stays the same. Which group fits now?","3|A blue square is turned on one corner. Which group still fits?"],t.s)
B.c7b=new A.bO(1,"Integrated exploration","Two Properties Can Sort One Object","Compare two properties together|Explain a sorting choice|Change a group when the rule changes",B.aqi,B.awy,"There are four trays. A blue circle cannot go with all blue objects if the rule uses shape too. Check color first: blue. Check shape next: round. Choose blue and round.","Where does a red square belong if the rule uses both color and shape?","Red and square. Red alone is not enough because there are two red groups.","Rotating a square card does not turn it into a circle. Use its edges, not its position.","A two-property rule needs both properties to match.",B.aMs)
B.asb=s(["Same starting line","Equal units","No gaps","Longer object"],t.s)
B.aps=s(["Start both objects at the same line. If one starts farther ahead, its end can mislead you.","Use units of the same size, such as equal paper squares. Large and small steps cannot be counted as if equal.","Place units end to end without spaces or overlaps. A gap counts empty space as part of the object.","With a shared start and equal units, the object reaching farther is longer. Length is not the same as color or weight."],t.s)
B.aOh=s(["0|Which rule fixes pencils that begin at different places?","1|Which rule fixes using large and small paper squares together?","2|Which rule fixes spaces left between measuring squares?","3|Two objects start together. Which label fits the one that reaches farther?","0|What should be checked before comparing the ends of two sticks?","1|What must be true of repeated blocks used as measuring units?","2|What placement rule prevents counting empty spaces?","3|One strip is seven equal units and another is five. Which label fits the seven-unit strip?","1|A table is four giant steps or eight tiny steps long. Which rule explains why counts alone do not compare length?","0|A shorter pencil seems to end farther away because it starts ahead. Which rule corrects the comparison?","2|A strip is measured with equal squares, but each pair has a space. Which rule is missing?"],t.s)
B.c7i=new A.bO(1,"Integrated exploration","Comparing Length Fairly","Line up objects to compare length|Use equal repeated units|Explain a fair measurement",B.asb,B.aps,"Two pencils begin at one line. One reaches six paper units; the other reaches four. Each unit is equal with no gaps. Six is greater than four, so the first is longer.","One child uses tiny steps and another uses giant steps. What measurement rule needs fixing?","Equal units. Step counts cannot be compared fairly when the steps differ in size.","A bigger number does not always mean a longer object if the measuring units differ.","A fair length comparison uses one start and equal units placed end to end.",B.aOh)
B.aSa=s(["Water","Food","Air","Suitable shelter"],t.s)
B.aSU=s(["Living things need water. Give a pet clean drinking water. Plants take in water mainly through roots.","Animals need suitable food. A pet needs food meant for that animal. Green plants use light to make their own food.","Living things need air for life processes. Never shut an animal in an airtight box.","A suitable shelter gives protection and enough space. A pet needs a safe home, not a closed jar."],t.s)
B.ase=s(["0|Which need is met by filling a clean drinking bowl?","1|Which need is met by giving a pet its proper meal?","2|Which need explains why a pet must not be sealed in a box?","3|Which need is met by a safe home that protects a pet from bad weather?","0|Roots taking liquid from damp soil meet which need?","1|A hungry animal needs which item from the model?","2|Breathing needs which item around us?","3|A nest protects young birds. Which need does it help meet?","0|A pet ate but its bowl has been empty all day. Which need is missing?","2|A child proposes an airtight home for a small pet. Which need would that plan fail?","3|A pet has food and water but no safe place during heavy rain. Which need remains?"],t.s)
B.c7p=new A.bO(2,"Integrated exploration","Caring for Plants and Pets","Identify basic needs|Match care to an observed need|Avoid harming plants and animals",B.aSa,B.aSU,"A pet has food but an empty water bowl. Food does not replace water. Ask an adult to refill the bowl with clean water.","A plant has water and air but is kept in a dark cupboard. Can its food making continue well?","No. Green leaves need light to make food. Water alone does not meet every need.","Do not feed wild animals or bring them home. Observe from a distance and protect their habitat.","Care means meeting several needs, not giving only one thing.",B.ase)
B.b1X=s(["Eye care","Ear care","Skin care","Food and clean water"],t.s)
B.ay2=s(["Eye care includes enough light for reading and keeping sharp objects away. Never look directly at the Sun.","Ear care includes moving away from loud noise. Do not push objects inside ears to clean them.","Skin care includes washing hands with soap and clean water. Dry hands with a clean towel.","Different nutritious foods and clean drinking water help the whole body. Sweets alone do not meet all food needs."],t.s)
B.aZi=s(["0|Which care choice includes keeping sharp pencils away from the face?","1|Which care choice includes avoiding very loud speakers?","2|Which care choice includes washing dirty hands?","3|Which care choice includes a varied nutritious meal?","0|Which choice explains using comfortable light to read?","1|Which choice explains not putting beads inside ears?","2|Which choice fits cleaning hands before a meal?","3|Which choice includes drinking safe water when thirsty?","1|A child says ears are safe because they do not bleed near loud noise. Which care topic corrects that idea?","0|A friend suggests watching the Sun through dark glasses. Which care topic explains refusing?","2|Hands look only a little dirty after gardening. Which care choice is still needed before eating?"],t.s)
B.c7a=new A.bO(2,"Integrated exploration","Healthy Habits Protect Our Senses","Match body parts to safe care|Explain why loud sound is harmful|Describe a healthy daily choice",B.b1X,B.ay2,"Ben handles soil, then wants a snack. He first washes his hands with soap and clean water. This removes dirt and many germs before eating.","A speaker is painfully loud. Which care choice fits?","Ear care: move farther away and tell an adult. Ears can be harmed even when no wound is seen.","Looking at the Sun through sunglasses is still unsafe. Do not try it.","Care for each body part and choose food and water that support the whole body.",B.aZi)
B.b11=s(["Start moving","Slow or stop","Change direction","Change shape"],t.s)
B.axF=s(["A gentle push can start a resting toy moving when it overcomes resistance from the surface.","A push against a moving toy can slow it or stop it. Keep fingers away from wheels and use only slow toys.","A sideways push can turn a moving object. Its path changes even if it is still moving.","A gentle squeeze can change the shape of a soft sponge. Some objects change shape more easily than others."],t.s)
B.aQ5=s(["0|A resting toy begins to travel after a gentle push. Which change happened?","1|A moving ball comes to rest against a cushion. Which change happened?","2|A slow toy turns after a sideways push. Which change happened?","3|A soft sponge becomes flatter when pressed. Which change happened?","0|A toy wagon was still, then a pull sets it moving. Which change fits?","1|A gently rolling ball loses speed on a rough mat. Which change fits?","2|A toy car goes left rather than straight ahead. Which change fits?","3|A soft clean cloth is folded. Which change fits?","2|A ball keeps moving but takes a new path. Which change must have occurred?","1|A force acts opposite a slowly moving toy. Its speed falls. Which change fits?","3|A sponge stays on one spot but is squeezed thinner. Which change shows a force acted?"],t.s)
B.c7L=new A.bO(3,"Integrated exploration","Pushes Pulls and Changes in Motion","Predict the effect of a gentle force|Identify starting and stopping|Describe a change in direction",B.b11,B.axF,"A toy ball is at rest. A gentle push starts it. Another gentle push from the side makes it turn. The two pushes produce different changes.","A soft sponge is squeezed gently. It becomes flatter. What changed?","Its shape changed. It need not travel across a table for a force to have an effect.","A force is not only something that makes objects faster. It can slow, turn, or reshape them.","A push or pull can change motion or shape.",B.aQ5)
B.aBJ=s(["Save water","Save paper","Save electricity","Ask an adult for safety"],t.s)
B.aJN=s(["Turn a tap fully off after washing. Water is needed by people, plants, and animals. Report leaks to an adult.","Use both sides of clean paper when possible. This reduces the amount of new paper needed.","Switch off unneeded lights with dry hands if an adult says it is safe. Electricity supplies useful light and movement.","Tell an adult about broken wires, sockets, or leaking electrical equipment. Children must not repair or test them."],t.s)
B.b03=s(["0|Which action is helped by closing a dripping tap?","1|Which action is helped by drawing on the blank back of a sheet?","2|Which action is helped by turning off an unneeded safe light?","3|Which choice fits finding a damaged socket?","0|A bucket catches safe rinse water for an adult to use on plants. Which resource is saved?","1|Reusing a clean sheet for a drawing saves which resource?","2|Leaving no empty-room light on saves which resource?","3|A child notices a wire beside water. Which choice must come first?","1|Two drawing plans work equally well. One uses a partly blank old sheet. Which saving choice fits?","0|A tap continues running after handwashing. Which action is needed?","3|A lamp is broken, and the switch feels wet. Which choice is safer than touching it?"],t.s)
B.c7Y=new A.bO(3,"Integrated exploration","Saving Water Paper and Electricity","Identify a wasted resource|Choose a safe conserving action|Explain one link between resources and nature",B.aBJ,B.aJN,"One side of a clean sheet is blank. Drawing there uses the sheet again. It saves paper without needing a new sheet.","A wire is broken near a lamp. Should a child touch it to stop wasted electricity?","No. Keep away and tell an adult. Safety comes before trying to save electricity.","Never touch sockets or wires to check whether electricity is flowing.","Use only what is needed and choose safety before repair.",B.b03)
B.aW3=s(["Rain record","Wind record","Cloud record","Safety response"],t.s)
B.avx=s(["A rain record notes when rain falls. Three rainy days are observations, not proof it will rain every day.","A wind record notes moving-air clues such as a flag waving. Observe from a safe place; do not go out in strong wind.","A cloud record notes how much sky is covered. Clouds can be present without rain at that moment.","A safety response uses the latest conditions and adult advice. Thunder means going into a safe building, not finishing outdoor play."],t.s)
B.awN=s(["0|Which record notes drops falling from clouds?","1|Which record notes flags waving in moving air?","2|Which record notes how much sky is covered?","3|Which part includes going indoors when thunder starts?","0|A chart counts two wet afternoons. Which kind of record is that?","1|A child draws arrows for the way a flag blows. Which record fits?","2|A child shades a sky drawing to show cloud cover. Which record fits?","3|An adult cancels outdoor play after a warning. Which part fits?","0|Monday and Tuesday have rain symbols and Wednesday has none. Which record can show two rainy days?","2|The sky has clouds but no rain falls. Which record can still include that observation?","3|The morning drawing shows sunshine, but thunder starts now. Which model part should guide action?"],t.s)
B.c7T=new A.bO(4,"Integrated exploration","Weather Records Tell a Story","Record a daily weather clue|Compare observations over days|Choose a safe response to changing weather",B.aW3,B.avx,"A chart shows rain on Monday and Tuesday but none on Wednesday. Count two rainy days. Do not label all three days rainy just because two match.","A cloudy morning becomes stormy in the afternoon. Which should guide what to do now: the old drawing or current warnings?","Current warnings. Records help us compare, but a safety response must use the newest conditions.","One rainy afternoon does not describe the weather for an entire month.","Record what happens, compare fairly, and respond to current weather safely.",B.awN)
B.aT5=s(["Soil","Water","Plants","Clean shared spaces"],t.s)
B.aVU=s(["Soil supports many plant roots. It contains bits of rock and old living material. Do not put soil in your mouth.","Water supports life. A stream is also a home for living things, not a place to throw rubbish.","Plants provide food and shade. Leaves use light to make food. Care for plants without breaking their stems.","Clean shared spaces reduce litter that can harm living things or block drains. Let adults handle sharp or unknown waste."],t.s)
B.b0j=s(["0|Which resource holds many plant roots?","1|Which resource fills a stream?","2|Which living things can provide shade?","3|Which model part includes putting litter in proper bins?","0|Which resource contains small rock pieces and old living material?","1|Which resource must be kept free from dumped rubbish in rivers?","2|Which living things make food using leaves and light?","3|Which model part includes keeping a school path free of litter?","1|A fish lives in a stream. Which resource is its immediate home?","0|A seedling needs a place for roots to hold on and take in water. Which resource provides that place?","3|Litter can wash through a drain into a stream. Which care action helps prevent that?"],t.s)
B.c8e=new A.bO(4,"Integrated exploration","People Plants and Our Surroundings","Recognize natural resources|Explain why soil and water matter|Describe a safe care action",B.aT5,B.aVU,"Rubbish beside a drain may wash into a stream. Keeping it in a proper bin helps both the shared space and the water habitat.","A young plant is growing beside a path. What should you avoid doing?","Do not pull it up or break its stem. Plants need their parts to keep growing.","Do not pick up sharp rubbish with bare hands. Ask an adult.","Our surroundings supply living things with places and resources to live.",B.b0j)
B.ayD=s([B.c7b,B.c7i,B.c7p,B.c7a,B.c7L,B.c7Y,B.c7T,B.c8e],t.EM)
