B.bgv=new A.cj("ai-source","ai-study.source",B.at,"For free offline Mathematics practice, choose Native Engine in the generator. It supports the listed topics, Foundation difficulty and English; completed exercises are excluded unless you allow repeats. Native quizzes save on this device and resume checked progress. For source-based AI, add a useful title and optional topic tag. Paste a clear paragraph or choose Upload and a supported file. Cloud uploads are limited to 10 MB. The experimental Local Study Generator accepts pasted notes only, between 80 and 16,000 characters; its runtime must be running on this computer.",B.hP,null,"Prepare your source","",null,"")
B.bgF=new A.cj("ai-mode","ai-study.mode",B.ea,"Choose an available practice mode, then an enabled item count. Multiple Choice offers answer options; Identification asks you to type; Flashcards are for reveal-and-review; Random Mix combines supported styles. True/false is unavailable in local mode. Disabled premium options cannot be selected.",B.jy,null,"Pick the question style and count","",null,"")
B.bgk=new A.cj("ai-generate","ai-study.generate",B.ea,"Choose Generate Study Set once and wait for the saved deck. Local requests show queue position or accepted-card progress and may take several minutes. If the connection fails, retry with exactly the same notes and settings to reconnect while the job is retained. Cloud generation requires a configured service and signed-in account.",B.jy,null,"Generate and handle waiting","",null,"")
B.bgO=new A.cj("ai-quality",null,B.at,"AI can return fewer usable questions than requested and can choose ambiguous wording or wrong distractors. Open Compare answers with source in a saved deck, including flashcard-only decks. Check each retained excerpt, answer and explanation, or flag a card for correction. Your comparisons save on this device for the current learner; edits to the question or its source require a fresh comparison. Missing excerpts cannot be confirmed for graded practice. Edit or delete weak cards. Native Mathematics uses computational checks and does not need this learner comparison. Source preservation is not proof of educational accuracy, and generated material is not a substitute for a trusted reference.",B.aH,null,"Check generated content","",null,"")
B.bgj=new A.cj("ai-privacy",null,B.at,"Use material you are allowed to upload. Avoid private student records and other sensitive information. Cloud and local storage are different: local AI saves notes and decks unencrypted on this computer and caches decks in the browser. Local mode is not a shared, authenticated classroom service.",B.aH,null,"Protect your material","",null,"")
B.aUQ=s([B.bgv,B.bgF,B.bgk,B.bgO,B.bgj],t.eT)
B.bg1=new A.ha("ai-study.v1",B.aUQ,"Create an AI study set")
B.bgh=new A.cj("library-find",null,B.at,"Open your study library from the AI study area. Search by the available title/topic fields and use the due-review filter to find cards needing attention. Open a deck to see its source, question count, and review/practice actions. If loading fails, use Retry; an error is not proof that your library is empty.",B.aH,null,"Find a saved study set","",null,"")
B.bh1=new A.cj("library-edit",null,B.at,"Inside a deck, Search cards filters its contents. The plus button adds a flashcard. Open a card action menu to edit or delete that card. Keep the prompt, answer, explanation, and source excerpt consistent. The card editor lets you retain or correct the excerpt from your original material. A missing excerpt leaves the card unverified; ungraded recall remains available. Review changes before using the card to grade yourself.",B.aH,null,"Search, add, and correct cards","",null,"")
B.bgY=new A.cj("library-delete",null,B.at,"The trash button on a study-set page deletes the deck, not just the current card. Read the confirmation before proceeding. Deletion removes the saved deck from the app; it is not an undo operation. Local AI job records can retain a generated result until their retention period expires.",B.aH,null,"Delete carefully","",null,"")
B.aQ6=s([B.bgh,B.bh1,B.bgY],t.eT)
B.bg0=new A.ha("library.v2",B.aQ6,"Study library & card editing")
B.bgn=new A.cj("review-due",null,B.at,"Review due cards limits the session to scheduled cards that need review now. Browse flashcards lets you inspect the deck without treating it as a scored quiz. A pure flashcard deck has Start Practice disabled; use the review or browse actions instead.",B.aH,null,"Due review or browsing","",null,"")
B.bgU=new A.cj("review-reveal",null,B.at,"Read the prompt and answer from memory before choosing Reveal. Compare your answer with the saved answer and source. Self-rating is for scheduling, not proof that an answer is correct, and it does not award quiz XP.",B.aH,null,"Recall before revealing","",null,"")
B.bgV=new A.cj("review-rate",null,B.at,"Choose Again if you could not recall the answer, Hard if recall took effort, or Got it if you remembered confidently. These ratings adjust future review timing. Be honest instead of choosing Got it just to finish. Review schedules saved locally should not be assumed to sync across devices.",B.aH,null,"Again, Hard, or Got it","",null,"")
B.aBT=s([B.bgn,B.bgU,B.bgV],t.eT)
B.bfZ=new A.ha("review.v2",B.aBT,"Flashcards & spaced review")
B.bgz=new A.cj("qa-source",null,B.at,"Open a deck and choose Ask Norie About This Source. Type one specific question and send it. This uses that deck's source, not every document in your library. Read the returned quote and check that it actually answers your question.",B.aH,null,"Ask about a saved source","",null,"")
B.bgR=new A.cj("qa-limits",null,B.at,"If the source does not support an answer, Norie may abstain. Rephrase a vague question or use a better source rather than treating an unsupported response as fact. Cloud Q&A needs connectivity and service access; local Q&A needs the local server, model, and saved source on this computer.",B.aH,null,"Missing evidence or an unavailable service","",null,"")
B.bgc=new A.cj("qa-help",null,B.at,"Ask Norie in the app shell handles directions and feature questions. Ask how to find a lesson, understand XP, or start this tutorial. For a factual question about study material, open the relevant saved source instead. Help & Support in the menu opens the complete guide.",B.aH,null,"App help is different","",null,"")
