B.aEy=s(["https://www.deped.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/English-CG.pdf | LEGACY May 2016 English Grade 9, PDF pp.202\u2013204, Q1: British-American including Philippine literary study, self-discovery, word order and conventions; workshop scene and poetic-inversion exercises.","https://www.deped.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/English-CG.pdf | LEGACY May 2016 English Grade 9, PDF pp.205\u2013208, Q2: interpreting literary/dramatic texts, expression and context; rehearsal drama. Actual British-American and Philippine literary works need additional contextualized reading.","https://www.deped.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/English-CG.pdf | LEGACY May 2016 English Grade 9, PDF pp.209\u2013211, Q3: one-act play analysis/performance and verbals, plus processing persuasive information; print-room scene and quiet-corner proposal. A short script is not a complete staged performance.","https://www.deped.gov.ph/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/English-CG.pdf | LEGACY May 2016 English Grade 9, PDF pp.212\u2013215, Q4: full-length play, consistent tense, modals, voice/reported speech and evaluation of reasoning/bias; three-act outline, performance reviews and supplementary calendar essay plan. Full-length script/performance not supplied; these are legacy skill selections, not current MATATAG quarter certification."],t.s)
