B.aZC=s(["Light passes through the thin specimen on a slide supported by the stage.","The lens close to the specimen forms the first magnified image.","The viewing lens magnifies that image further.","Focus adjusts the separation for a clear image; arm and base support the instrument."],t.s)
B.bEx=new A.ap("A compound light microscope combines lenses and careful support","comparison",B.b0u,B.aZC,"Simplified classroom transmitted-light model, not an optical ray tracing or measured instrument drawing. Begin at low power and follow teacher instructions to protect the slide and objective.",B.u,"","g7-microscope")
B.au1=s(["100\xd7 total","400\xd7 total","Size estimate"],t.s)
B.aCK=s(["A supplied calibrated field diameter is 4.0 mm.","With the same eyepiece setup, four times the magnification gives an approximately 1.0 mm field diameter.","Four equal cell widths spanning a 1.0 mm diameter suggest about 0.25 mm, or 250 \u03bcm, per cell."],t.s)
B.bEM=new A.ap("More magnification usually means a smaller specimen field","comparison",B.au1,B.aCK,"Example calibration, not a universal field size for every microscope. Magnification enlarges the image; it does not enlarge the actual cells or automatically improve resolution.",B.u,"","")
B.aH5=s(["Repeated boundaries","Dark stained region","Unseen small structure"],t.s)
B.b0A=s(["A supplied plant micrograph may show cell-wall outlines; a membrane may not be separately resolved.","A labeled prepared image can identify a nucleus; stain color alone is not a species test.","A mitochondrion drawn in a model may not be distinguishable in a classroom image; invisibility is not absence."],t.s)
B.bED=new A.ap("A micrograph is evidence; a cell diagram is an explanatory model","comparison",B.aH5,B.b0A,"Use the image key, scale and sample description. Dye and diagram colors improve contrast rather than establishing natural colors or exact shapes.",B.u,"","")
B.aR1=s(["Changed variable","Measured outcome","Controlled conditions"],t.s)
